									class Value
									{
										class data
										{
											singleType="STRING";
											value="Following the collapse of the Soviet Union in 1991, Chernarus was amongst one of the many ex-Soviet territories to regain its independence.     " \n "<br/><br/>      " \n "However, pro-Russian citizens would unite to form an opposition party as the so-called Chernarussian Movement of the Red Star (ChDKZ). The ChDKZ and its supporters vowed to challenge the ruling pro-West Party; their ultimate goal being full integration with Russia.     " \n "<br/><br/>      " \n "In response to its rise, anti-ChDKZ radicals rallied together to form the National Party (NAPA), vowing to stamp out the ChDKZ and its supporters. Skirmishes between supporters on both sides, including Government forces would gradually escalate into bloody civil war.     " \n "<br/><br/>      " \n "In 2015, Russia launched a full scale invasion with the goal of 'restoring order', in support of the ChDKZ. Russian soldiers crossed the border into Chernarus from all sides, striking from Takistan, the Green Sea and the Russian border.   ";
										};
									};
								};
